# 14. DETECTION RULES

A detection rule defines conditions that may indicate suspicious activity.

Examples:

### Brute-force detection

```text
Many failed logins
+
Same account/source
+
Short time window
```

### Impossible-travel-style detection

```text
Login from Location A
+
Login from distant Location B
+
Impossible time difference
```

This requires validation because VPNs, proxies, mobile networks, and legitimate travel can create false positives.

---

# 15. FALSE POSITIVE

SIEM reports suspicious activity but it is legitimate.

Example:

```text
Many login attempts
      ↓
Investigation
      ↓
Approved vulnerability scanner
```

Result:

> False positive.

---

# 16. FALSE NEGATIVE

Malicious activity occurs but the SIEM does not detect it.

This is dangerous because:

> **The organization may not know the attack is occurring.**

