# 27. COMMON SIEM PROBLEMS

### Alert fatigue

Too many alerts.

### Poor logging

Important data missing.

### Bad time synchronization

Timeline becomes unreliable.

### Poor correlation

Related events are not connected.

### Excessive collection

Too much irrelevant data.

### Missing context

Alert lacks useful information.

---

# 28. HOW TO REDUCE ALERT FATIGUE

- Tune rules
- Remove unnecessary alerts
- Prioritize severity
- Add context
- Correlate multiple events
- Suppress known benign activity carefully
- Review detection performance

